Subject: [PATCH] drop apr_pool_mutex_set call for APR >= 1.7

apr_pool_mutex_set() only exists on APR development branches between
1.x and 2.0 (and was never shipped in any released APR). UniMRCP 1.8.0
calls it unconditionally inside OWN_ALLOCATOR_PER_POOL, which breaks
the link step on every distro-packaged APR (1.6, 1.7).

apr_allocator_mutex_set() on the preceding line already gives the
allocator the mutex it needs. Dropping the call preserves behavior.

Tested on Ubuntu 22.04, APR 1.7.0.

Apply from the UniMRCP source root with:
    patch -p1 < 0001-drop-apr-pool-mutex-set.patch

--- a/libs/apr-toolkit/src/apt_pool.c
+++ b/libs/apr-toolkit/src/apt_pool.c
@@ -38,7 +38,6 @@
 			apr_allocator_owner_set(allocator,pool);
 			apr_thread_mutex_create(&mutex,APR_THREAD_MUTEX_NESTED,pool);
 			apr_allocator_mutex_set(allocator,mutex);
-			apr_pool_mutex_set(pool,mutex); 
 		}
 	}
 #else
